These admin flows depend on `GET /upload/actions/generate-ai-metadata/latest` returning the latest job record. With the cron removed, they will see historical completed/failed jobs as long as they exist in the DB.

**Effect on entrypoints:** user-visible behavior for “latest job status” remains the same for fresh jobs; the difference is in DB housekeeping rather than immediate response semantics. However, over very long time, old jobs will accumulate, which could have operational impact (storage, potential performance of queries on the job table, etc.), but that cannot be quantified from code alone.

